"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,928\nThe Learning Brain\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,505\nEpisode 15\n\n3\n00:00:07,585 --> 00:00:10,229\nAdult plasticity and belief\n\n4\n00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:18,113\nAdults with no juggling experience spent three months learning a three-ball cascade.\n\n5\n00:00:18,737 --> 00:00:23,469\nBrain scans showed more grey matter in an area that tracks visual motion.\n\n6\n00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,226\nThree months after they stopped practicing,\n\n7\n00:00:26,482 --> 00:00:28,241\nmuch of that increase had faded.\n\n8\n00:00:28,411 --> 00:00:30,418\nSo adult brains do change.\n\n9\n00:00:30,615 --> 00:00:32,099\nBut notice three things.\n\n10\n00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:33,813\nThe change was specific: a motion area,\n\n11\n00:00:33,955 --> 00:00:36,097\nfor a motion skill.\n\n12\n00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:38,480\nIt took months of effortful practice.\n\n13\n00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:40,365\nAnd without use, it receded.\n\n14\n00:00:40,824 --> 00:00:43,294\nSome windows also narrow with age,\n\n15\n00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:45,593\nlike learning a new language without an accent.\n\n16\n00:00:46,141 --> 00:00:47,993\nAdult plasticity is real,\n\n17\n00:00:48,013 --> 00:00:49,310\nbut it is earned,\n\n18\n00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,053\nspecific, and kept by use.\n\n19\n00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:52,778\nThis is where belief comes in.\n\n20\n00:00:53,272 --> 00:00:56,369\nGrowth mindset is the idea that ability can be developed,\n\n21\n00:00:56,763 --> 00:00:58,627\nand in one sense it is simply true.\n\n22\n00:00:59,077 --> 00:01:01,472\nBut do brief mindset lessons raise grades?\n\n23\n00:01:01,493 --> 00:01:01,719\nIn the largest trial,\n\n24\n00:01:02,015 --> 00:01:05,593\nwith more than twelve thousand ninth graders,\n\n25\n00:01:05,836 --> 00:01:11,545\ntwo short online sessions raised lower achieving students' grades by about a tenth of a grade point.\n\n26\n00:01:12,142 --> 00:01:15,213\nMeta-analyses find small average effects.\n\n27\n00:01:15,597 --> 00:01:20,126\nOne that kept only the highest quality studies found an effect near zero.\n\n28\n00:01:20,296 --> 00:01:22,386\nSo be careful in both directions.\n\n29\n00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:26,041\nDo not promise that belief alone produces learning.\n\n30\n00:01:26,401 --> 00:01:29,305\nAnd do not tell students their abilities are fixed.\n\n31\n00:01:29,576 --> 00:01:31,041\nBoth claims are wrong.\n\n32\n00:01:31,211 --> 00:01:31,991\nFor teaching.\n\n33\n00:01:32,407 --> 00:01:36,743\nTell students the honest version: skills grow with the right kind of practice,\n\n34\n00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:37,487\nover time.\n\n35\n00:01:37,893 --> 00:01:39,611\nPraise strategy and progress,\n\n36\n00:01:39,631 --> 00:01:40,817\nnot effort alone.\n\n37\n00:01:41,249 --> 00:01:43,723\nEffort that is not working needs a new strategy,\n\n38\n00:01:43,743 --> 00:01:45,009\nnot more of the same.\n\n39\n00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,420\nShow students their own growth,\n\n40\n00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,326\nearly work beside later work.\n\n41\n00:01:49,653 --> 00:01:52,602\nAnd design courses where improvement is possible,\n\n42\n00:01:52,776 --> 00:01:55,373\nwith chances to revise and try again.\n\n43\n00:01:55,543 --> 00:01:57,017\nThe brain can change.\n\n44\n00:01:57,256 --> 00:01:58,717\nBelief opens the door.\n\n45\n00:01:58,924 --> 00:02:01,722\nPractice, strategy, and time do the work.\n\n"
